# Security rules

Full model: `@SECURITY.md` and `@docs/SECURITY.md`. Privacy ops: `@docs/PRIVACY.md`.

## Never

- Commit secrets, tokens, or real `DATABASE_URL` / Clerk / CSRF values.
- Log PII, tokens, or full auth headers.
- Disable CSRF, auth, or rate limiting to “make tests pass” in production code paths.
- Trust client-supplied user IDs for privileged actions without `getVerifiedAuth` / `requireRole` checks.

## Required production env (do not invent alternatives)

- `DATABASE_URL`
- `CLERK_SECRET_KEY`
- `VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`
- `CSRF_SECRET` (min 32 chars in production)

Optional: `SENTRY_DSN`, `LOG_LEVEL`, `HTTPS_ONLY`, `BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN` (proof uploads).

## Uploads

Certification proofs go through `POST /api/certifications/proof` → Vercel Blob. Keep PDF/JPEG/PNG + size limits; do not broaden file types without an explicit security review.

## Headers

Apply security headers via `@src/lib/securityHeaders.server.ts` (`applySecurityHeaders`) on responses that already do so — keep CSP/HSTS behavior intact.
